Needs:
* Node v14.6.0 >=
* (optional, to rebuild jsetimos.js) npm; build_ts.sh installs the pinned
  typescript 3.8.3 (future versions add unwanted transpiled code) by itself

To try:
Open index.html in a browser.

To run a file:
node jsetimos.js fileName

To run in shell mode (REPL):
node jsetimos.js

To run from raw input (untested):
node jsetimos.js --inputMode "print("hello")"

Import files:
    Base dir is main file running directory.
    "import a.b" looks for a/b.jk next to the importing file first,
    then from the base dir (e.g. "import stdlib.math" works from tests/).
    JSEtimos file extension is *.jk

TypeScript implementation (src/typescript, compiled into ./jsetimos.js):
If you made some changes on src/typescript/jsetimos.ts you need to recompile it.
./build_ts.sh           builds ./jsetimos.js
./build_ts.sh --test    builds and runs the unit and bug regression tests

Go implementation (src/go, needs Go 1.21 or newer):
./build_go.sh           builds ./jsetimos (jsetimos.exe on Windows)
./build_go.sh --test    builds and runs the unit and bug regression tests

Bug regression tests (one file per fixed bug in tests/bugs):
tests/bugs/run.sh [node|go|both]

If you want some syntax highlight when editing 
jsetimos code you can use the kotlin highlighter
of your editor of choice, will work well enough.

